 1\\end{aligned}]}.$" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350461 1113 #uuid "12cb29bf-f056-51b7-aa00-a244ffe6e6cf" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350461 1145 "We start by creating a matrix whose columns are made up of our vectors, and then we reduce the matrix to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, our matrix is already in a row echelon form.\n\nThe pivot columns correspond to basis vectors, while the non-pivot columns correspond to linearly dependent vectors that can be removed. Here, the reduced matrix has $4$ pivot columns (or alternatively, $4$ non-zero rows). \n\nTherefore, the dimension of the span is $4.$" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350462 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350463 13194139535461 true] [17592186350462 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350464 13194139535461 true] [17592186350462 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350465 13194139535461 true] [17592186350462 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350466 13194139535461 true] [17592186350462 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350467 13194139535461 true] [17592186350462 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535461 true] [17592186350462 1041 "selection" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350462 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350466 13194139535461 true] [17592186350462 1110 #uuid "2d39f96b-cb50-5b97-8744-a6dfd6d30bcd" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350463 1034 "3" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350463 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535461 true] [17592186350463 1111 #uuid "ea8e400c-4cb8-5b95-b5d2-de18dac61c50" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350464 1034 "2" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350464 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535461 true] [17592186350464 1111 #uuid "4533b8b1-0e73-573d-88b1-1e1176acfb5e" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350465 1034 "1" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350465 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535461 true] [17592186350465 1111 #uuid "7803d8b1-9764-5187-9445-246a598082b3" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350466 1034 "4" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350466 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535461 true] [17592186350466 1111 #uuid "4e9f7ebd-52bf-5b0c-889f-0bd17c6af181" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350467 1034 "0" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350467 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535461 true] [17592186350467 1111 #uuid "38c4fd6d-a531-57d7-b0b0-876303d4220a" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350468 1017 #edb/ref 17592186350469 13194139535461 true] [17592186350468 1089 "q-79323" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350468 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535461 true] [17592186350468 1100 "Let ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ be linearly independent vectors, and suppose that the vector $w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ form a basis of $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w}$\n- $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}})=3$\n- $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w})=3$" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350468 1113 #uuid "77009195-0b55-53e1-b37a-b9c64dc878fc" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350468 1145 "Recall that a basis of a vector space $V$ is a set of linearly independent vectors that span $V.$ The dimension of $V$ is the number of vectors in any basis of $V$ (if such a basis exists). \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. We are told that $w$ can be written as a linear combination of ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}.$ This means that $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w}$ is completely spanned by the vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ only, and we are told that ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ are linearly independent vectors. So, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ is a basis of the span.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, $\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is spanned by ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$, and these are linearly independent vectors. So, ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ is a basis of the span.Therefore, we have $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}})=3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}$ is a basis of the given span and this basis contains $3$ vectors, we have $\\text{dim}(\\text{Span}{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3},w})=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350469 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350470 13194139535461 true] [17592186350469 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350471 13194139535461 true] [17592186350469 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350472 13194139535461 true] [17592186350469 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350473 13194139535461 true] [17592186350469 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350474 13194139535461 true] [17592186350469 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535461 true] [17592186350469 1041 "selection" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350469 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350470 13194139535461 true] [17592186350469 1110 #uuid "6b0023e2-cac4-56ad-9a03-7b5ce3a018b6" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350470 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350470 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535461 true] [17592186350470 1111 #uuid "cc5b635d-71dd-594e-9fc1-60d35844414d" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350471 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350471 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535461 true] [17592186350471 1111 #uuid "9f3dfa4e-7a61-55f2-b5f8-f68003697e8d" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350472 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350472 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535461 true] [17592186350472 1111 #uuid "5ba19d77-fd3a-5d71-934b-f082f41e05f9" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350473 1034 "I only" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350473 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535461 true] [17592186350473 1111 #uuid "0027c121-006e-599d-8e5b-6af6f356fe95" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350474 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535461 true] [17592186350474 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535461 true] [17592186350474 1111 #uuid "18e2108f-46f0-5959-b16f-37710999436d" 13194139535461 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-159784"